Class Diagram

A Class Diagram is a UML (Unified Modeling Language) diagram used to represent the structure of a system by showing:

Classes
Attributes
Methods
Relationships between classes

It is the most important diagram in Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).

Definition

A Class Diagram describes:

Static structure of a system
Objects and their relationships
Data members and functions of classes

It helps developers design software architecture before coding.

Main Components of Class Diagram
1. Class

A class is a blueprint for creating objects.

